# Copy to .env. studio.sh reads these names and nothing else; no value ever
# reaches the command line, and none of them reach the page — the browser talks
# to studio.sh, and studio.sh talks to the model.
#
# Pick ONE of the blocks below. Everything in the editor works without any of
# them; only the AI panels go quiet.

# ── A model on your own machine ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# No key: there is nobody to authenticate to, and nothing you write leaves the
# machine — deck, figures and prompts all stay here. If one of these is already
# running when you start studio.sh, it is found without this file at all.
#
# Ollama          ollama serve && ollama pull qwen3:14b
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# STUDIO_MODEL=qwen3:14b
#
# LM Studio       start its local server from the Developer tab
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
# STUDIO_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-14b
#
# llama.cpp       llama-server -m model.gguf --port 8000
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# STUDIO_MODEL=local
#
# vLLM            vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-14B --port 8000
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# STUDIO_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-14B
#
# A 14B model draws a usable figure. Below about 7B the SVG tends to come back
# malformed, and the editor will tell you so rather than showing you a mess.

# ── Or a hosted one ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint works; the two named here are
# only the common ones.
#
# OpenAI
# OPENAI_KEY=sk-...
# STUDIO_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
#
# Anything else — OpenRouter, Together, Groq, an institutional gateway
# OPENAI_KEY=...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# STUDIO_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b
